# {{lb|de|of rental prices|chiefly adverbial or in compounds}} including [[heating]] [[cost]]s, [[water]], and [[fee]]s ([[electricity]] may or may not be included)
#: {{ux|de|Ich zahle 800&nbsp;€ '''warm''' für meine Wohnung.|I pay €800 for my apartment, including utilities.}}
# {{lb|de|dated|except in {{m|de|warmer Bruder}}}} [[gay]], [[homosexual]] (mostly male)
#: {{syn|de|schwul}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m+|de||warm}} means “warm”, but not “feeling warm”; therefore the phrase {{m|de||ich bin warm|lit=I am warm}} would mean that one’s body has a high temperature, particularly that one’s skin is warm on the outside. The English “I am warm” (that is: I <u>feel</u> warm) is equivalent to {{m+|de||mir ist warm|lit=to me it's warm}}.
* Although {{m|de||warm|gloss=gay}} is not in general use, this sense is current enough to make it advisable not to describe the relation between two men as {{m|de||warm}} (unless the implication is intended).

